  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Talk about languages",
   "texto": [
    "The Norwegian present does not change according to the person: jeg snakker and du snakker carry the same verbal form. In Spanish it does change: «I'm talking.», «You talk.».",
    "Norsk may be the «noruego/a» gentiicon or the name of the «noruego» language. The people and languages begin with a tiny one.",
    "The snakker form may mean «I'm talking.» or «estoy hablando»; the context clarifies the situation. There is no different progressive conjugation."
   ]
